Subject: Re: Follow-up: Integration & rate-limits (SDK, auth, retries, idempotency)

Hi Jane —

Thanks for the details, that traffic profile is helpful. Quick answers / recommendations from the infra side:

Rate-limit headers we emit (recommended clients should read these and behave accordingly)
- X-RateLimit-Limit: total allowed requests in the window
- X-RateLimit-Remaining: remaining requests
- X-RateLimit-Reset: epoch seconds when the window resets
- Retry-After: seconds to wait before retry (present on some 429 responses)

Recommended retry strategy (SDK + client best practice)
- If response includes Retry-After: honor the server-specified Retry-After (sleep that many seconds).
- Otherwise: use exponential backoff with jitter. Example: initial=500ms, multiplier=2.0, max_delay=8s, jitter=uniform(0, 250ms).
- Max attempts: 5 for transient errors (429, 503). For streaming/long-running ops use resumable/reconnect logic, not blind retries.

Idempotency and request IDs
- Include an Idempotency-Key header for any non-idempotent operation (e.g., create/save that must not be duplicated). Key semantics: up to 128 chars recommended; treat as opaque string.
- Include X-Request-ID on all requests for tracing — we echo this back in logs and error responses so you can correlate.
- We persist idempotency keys for 24 hours by default in Dedicated deployments; for Hosted we can negotiate retention for POC if needed.

Server-side quotas / routing
- We support per-route quotas and per-customer burst windows. For your POC, we can provision a 1.5x burst window to accommodate the 800 RPS spike.
- We recommend routing critical low-latency flows to a pinned model variant. Non-critical or batch reranks can route to lower-cost variants.

SDK snippet (pseudo-JS)

fetchWithRetries(url, opts = {}) {
  const maxAttempts = 5;
  const baseDelay = 500; // ms
  const idempotencyKey = opts.idempotencyKey || generateUuid();
  const requestId = opts.requestId || generateUuid();

  for (let attempt = 1; attempt <= maxAttempts; attempt++) {
    const res = await fetch(url, {
      ...opts,
      headers: {
        ...(opts.headers || {}),
        'Idempotency-Key': idempotencyKey,
        'X-Request-ID': requestId
      }
    });

    if (res.ok) return res;

    if (res.status === 429) {
      const retryAfter = res.headers.get('Retry-After');
      if (retryAfter) {
        await sleep(parseInt(retryAfter) * 1000);
        continue;
      }
    }

    if ([429, 502, 503].includes(res.status) && attempt < maxAttempts) {
      const jitter = Math.random() * 250;
      const delay = Math.min(baseDelay * Math.pow(2, attempt - 1) + jitter, 8000);
      await sleep(delay);
      continue;
    }

    // non-retryable or out of attempts
    throw new Error(`Request failed after ${attempt} attempts: ${res.status}`);
  }
}

Notes:
- For streams: we recommend keeping small heartbeats and reconnect with incremental resumption tokens.
- For embeddings/rerank workloads: batch small requests server-side to reduce per-request overhead; use bulk endpoints where possible.

